Cephes Math Library — 3-Clause BSD License
==========================================

This file exists because `mlx-gen-mage/src/latent.rs` (module `latent::cephes`)
contains a Rust port of the Cephes double-precision `ndtri` (inverse normal CDF)
and `erf`/`erfc` routines, including their coefficient tables verbatim. That is
production code and it DOES ship in binary bundles, so BSD-3 clauses 1 and 2
require the copyright notice, this list of conditions and the disclaimer below
to travel with both source and binary redistributions. See the "Ported
third-party source" section of the sibling `NOTICE` file for the attribution
entry and the rationale.

The grant relied upon is the one PyTorch reproduces for the same routines, in
the note `[3-Clause BSD License for the Cephes Math Library]` in
`aten/src/ATen/native/Math.h`. It is reproduced verbatim below (comment markers
removed, text unaltered). The Cephes source headers themselves carry the
copyright as "Copyright 1984, 1987, 1988, 1992, 2000 by Stephen L. Moshier";
the grant text below states it as "Copyright (c) 2018, Steven Moshier". Both
forms are recorded so neither is lost.

